# A print move straight across the bed's rotation axis is refused.  The
# bed angle is derived from the commanded x/y, so a path from (-40, 0) to
# (40, 0) turns the bed half a turn at the instant the sign of x flips -
# there is no rate there to slow down, and no feedrate makes a step take
# longer.  A travel move is routed through the centre instead (see
# polar_singularity.test), but that stops on the axis while the bed turns,
# which on a print move would leave a blob - so print_policy defaults to
# refusing.
#
# Note how little the arithmetic sees: the path's perpendicular offset
# from the centre is exactly zero, so every angular rate computed for it
# is zero while the bed still has half a turn to make.  It is the swept
# angle, not the rate, that catches this one.
CONFIG polar_singularity.cfg
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
SHOULD_FAIL

G28 X
G28 B
G28 Z
G90
G1 Z10 F600

# Round to the far side rather than across the middle, so that the only
# move this test refuses is the last one
G1 X0 Y40 F3000
G1 X-40 Y0 F3000

# And now straight back across it, extruding
G1 X40 Y0 E5 F3000
